{"body":"Stable offline candidates can now be bound to an external immutable audit Release and included with preview in a deterministic object-storage plan. The existing candidate archive, receipt, null IDs and signed APT/RPM bytes are preserved. Shared public entries remain owned by preview; stable RPM uses a mirrorlist pointing to one complete immutable snapshot.\n\nThe explicit stable path validates historical Git control/producer bytes, fresh source assets, attestations and native metadata, and actual candidate signatures before asset writes. Final source/main/tag/policy checks fence publication. TEST ONLY requires loopback endpoints and rejects redirects. Stable remains disabled; production workflows, manifests, keys, permissions and live hosting are unchanged.\n\nValidation on the final reviewed tree:\n\n- 468 Python tests completed successfully (one existing native RPM environment skip), plus four contract tests and the complete contract script.\n- The pinned Linux signing image passed 31 candidate cases plus eight transport cases, including signature checks after removal of test private material, loopback audit readback, deterministic composite output and retained-generation rejection.\n- Independent review found and closed a resolution-file read race with a failing regression before the fix. All 38 protected control/producer files remain byte-identical.\n- The first native attempt exited 137 with an unknown initiator; that failure is retained. The one unchanged isolated repeat and subsequent revision-bound runs passed.\n\nThis PR supplies sealing/transport capability and local validation. Actual production sealing, OSS/CDN activation and exact-version public-client acceptance remain outstanding. Both automatic Linux PR workflows passed on their first attempt: [Pages validation](https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/actions/runs/39587825259) ran all 468 Python tests without skips plus four contract tests; [native validation](https://github.com/WuKongIM/packages/actions/runs/39587825081) passed metadata 7, local signing 10, bootstrap 6, candidate 31 and transport 8 cases, followed by the complete signed preview APT/RPM repository drill. Actual checkout `873b760b734ace5d19d7f56d90ee053c83a3abac` has the same complete tree as head `59549efe1074562928b8ae175faeda8778849e0e`. The existing full repository drill uses fixed trusted product source `ed7e67d8f781b4f92872e42116c11b304fe03b5c`; it is not current-product or public stable acceptance. Pages configuration/upload/deployment were skipped.\n","headRefOid":"59549efe1074562928b8ae175faeda8778849e0e","isDraft":false,"state":"OPEN"}
